 "text": "Hi, how have you been? At least two weeks, four if it's thin oil paint. If you varnish too soon, the oil feels slow rather than fast. Then buy it for someone else, or a cheap pen and few sweets. Oil painting varnish isn' cheap, and it' worth waiting for. A quick coat of linseed oil instead of the varnish is faster, but still needs at least two weeks. Rub it with your fingernail, if it feels smooth like furniture wood instead of greasy it's dry.",
